1
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,100
Went out with my little brother — fun, was it?

2
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:11,030
2/10. Not really feeling it.

3
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:12,670
Friend's little brother?

4
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,800
Friend's little brother, my ass.

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,430
If we're only brothers, then why say you want to be together?

6
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:20,200
I'm thinking we throw a mini concert in the heart of Siam.

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,200
And ask FUN VIBE, our school band, to help out.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,000
I don't think I can stay till the end of your show, Star.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,070
How about we hold auditions? Let's do it.

10
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:30,070
Whoa-oh-oh. / Whoa-oh-oh.

11
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,530
I know who can help us.

12
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:36,200
I'll see him at school tonight.

13
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,470
Aren't you worried Mii will get hurt?

14
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Oh, shit!

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,230
3, 2, 1... Go.

16
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:48,870
And next time, if you really want to thank me, take me out for a meal.

17
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:54,270
I'm sorry. / But don't ever do that again.

18
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:56,970
I don't like being left behind. Especially by you.

19
00:00:56,970 --> 00:00:59,870
Why Star's name? I wanted it just between us.

20
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:01,370
Does this have to be such a big deal?

21
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:03,730
What hurts me is that my feelings

22
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,930
are such a small thing to you.

23
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:24,530
Fuen, you haven't left for school yet?

24
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:28,030
It's seven thirty, you're late. Want me to drop you off?

25
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,900
Then I'll go with you today, Mom.

26
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:40,070
All right, let's go. I'll drop you off.

27
00:05:11,530 --> 00:05:13,330
You had a fight with Fuen, huh?

28
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:21,200
I didn't even have to ask.

29
00:05:24,430 --> 00:05:27,400
So what, you're not going to make up?

30
00:05:31,930 --> 00:05:35,000
I will. Just not right now.

31
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:40,630
Come on, you're going to give in anyway.

32
00:05:40,630 --> 00:05:42,370
Do I have to pick the right moment too?

33
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:46,800
Since when do you play hard to get?

34
00:05:52,270 --> 00:05:56,700
I'm not. I'm just still upset.

35
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,330
Then stop asking me about it.

36
00:06:04,370 --> 00:06:07,270
When you snuck off to join the football club, I didn't say a word.

37
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,230
Big football star now, are we?

38
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:18,530
You already know?

39
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:22,470
Who ratted? Est? Jay? Or Zac?

40
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:28,230
Let's just say I know.

41
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,000
Are you mad?

42
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,170
I'm not mad.

43
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,170
Just don't go looking for trouble.

44
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:43,900
Careful, you'll get your wish — you'll be singing the blues.

45
00:06:47,130 --> 00:06:48,330
Bro.

46
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:51,670
The food's no good either.

47
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:54,200
Is it too salty?

48
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,170
It's because of you. / Hey.

49
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,570
If Mom made it too salty, just say so.

50
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:06,770
Fine, it's delicious. Satisfied.

51
00:07:08,170 --> 00:07:09,270
Quit messing with me.

52
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,830
Hey, be nice to your little brother.

53
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:15,700
Mom, he bit me. / Don't tell on me.

54
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,670
What, you're telling Mom over this? Ridiculous.

55
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:31,730
Hello, everyone. It's me. My name is Tonnam.

56
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:34,830
I'm representing Thapfah Wittayanusorn School.

57
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,830
Hey, Ton, you already dropped the promo clip?

58
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,100
I wasn't trying to show off.

59
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,430
You're showing off right now.

60
00:07:44,670 --> 00:07:49,000
And I'd like everyone to see how hard we've been practicing.

61
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,830
We've put our hearts into it, and we've given it everything.

62
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:55,830
Because we're about to have — have — have a concert in the heart of Siam.

63
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:58,700
And FUN VIBE, the band that just went viral,

64
00:07:58,700 --> 00:08:00,800
is coming to the show too, everyone.

65
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:06,930
We're putting this on to raise money for school activities.

66
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:10,300
We'd love for you all to come and have fun.

67
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:12,170
Because we'll have a blast, guaranteed.

68
00:08:12,170 --> 00:08:16,400
Come see us at Siam tonight, eight to ten.

69
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,670
Bring everyone you can.

70
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:21,330
No money? No problem. All you gotta bring is your heart.

71
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,930
What a headache.

72
00:08:33,730 --> 00:08:37,070
Now the rest is up to him.

73
00:08:38,169 --> 00:08:41,730
So? Any word on who he got to sing?

74
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:43,169
I already know.

75
00:08:43,970 --> 00:08:45,330
Go see for yourself.

76
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:48,730
Why?

77
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:51,200
It's a hell of a surprise.

78
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:53,400
That's all I'm saying.

79
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:16,930
How'd you like that? I put three past you on FIFA last night.

80
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,700
Yesterday they were all over each other,

81
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:37,530
and today what the hell happened?

82
00:09:38,770 --> 00:09:40,400
I saw it the same time you did.

83
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:43,770
But those two have never fought before, that's the thing.

84
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:47,570
Right? It's normal. He's always fighting with me.

85
00:09:47,570 --> 00:09:49,470
Now that I think about it, it does sting.

86
00:09:58,800 --> 00:09:59,830
Physics.

87
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,870
There's a concert tonight. Coming with us?

88
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:12,570
Nah. Not in the mood.

89
00:10:22,070 --> 00:10:25,170
Fuen, what about you?

90
00:10:34,930 --> 00:10:37,270
I'll let you know later.

91
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,770
I think it's serious.

92
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:16,570
Just play it the way we rehearsed. I don't think there'll be any problem.

93
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:17,970
Go all out.

94
00:11:19,770 --> 00:11:21,130
Don't worry, Star.

95
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:46,300
Star, there's something I want to talk to you about.

96
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,130
Yes?

97
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:09,370
Star, why did you bring in an outsider for our school's event?

98
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:13,170
If you couldn't find anyone, why not say so? Our school has plenty of singers.

99
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:17,900
I did look, but there was no one. And Rei was happy to help.

100
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:21,870
Besides, I thought it was for a good cause,

101
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:23,730
so I didn't think it was a problem.

102
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,170
It is.

103
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,330
This is our school's event.

104
00:12:36,330 --> 00:12:38,100
We shouldn't drag outsiders into it.

105
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,370
Drag them into what, Din? Rei hasn't even done anything yet.

106
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:48,400
And honestly, I don't get why you're picking a fight with me.

107
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:53,030
Star, change the singer. I'm asking you.

108
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:54,730
No.

109
00:12:55,230 --> 00:12:58,170
If that's your only reason, I don't want to change.

110
00:12:58,170 --> 00:13:02,130
I think what I said is as clear and reasonable as it gets.

111
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:04,730
If you're choosing to be stubborn

112
00:13:04,730 --> 00:13:06,670
just because you want to win, is that it?

113
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:15,270
No, that's not it.

114
00:13:15,270 --> 00:13:20,430
But I think the reason you're upset right now is that you're bringing something personal into this.

115
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:23,200
I know you and Rei had a falling out.

116
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,500
But that's got nothing to do with me, right?

117
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:28,630
Then suit yourself.

118
00:13:29,530 --> 00:13:31,330
If you think he won't walk out on you,

119
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:34,800
if you think he'll see it through, then go ahead.

120
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,230
But as for me...

121
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:49,970
he's someone who's always ready to cause trouble.

122
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,830
Should I pull out, Star?

123
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:20,970
It's fine, Rei. And don't think too much about it.

124
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:26,730
Let's leave rehearsal here for today. My friends have a match to get to.

125
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:31,930
Then before tonight, can I hold you to that meal you promised me?

126
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,500
I don't think he can.

127
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,170
Star's got a lot on his plate.

128
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:42,230
He's got to sort out moving the gear, the venue, the press, all of it.

129
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:46,630
He really can't. I'm sorry, truly.

130
00:14:47,230 --> 00:14:50,370
No worries. I'll head back to school for now.

131
00:14:50,370 --> 00:14:53,500
Once the show's done, I'll ask again.

132
00:14:57,170 --> 00:14:59,230
Should I walk you out?

133
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:00,870
You're busy, Star. It's fine.

134
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:03,270
Rei, this way, please.

135
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:41,870
Why did it go that way?

136
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:46,070
I just — I kicked it straight, I had my eye on the ball. Boom!

137
00:15:47,470 --> 00:15:49,270
Because you don't watch the ball.

138
00:15:49,830 --> 00:15:53,830
Come on, if I'm shooting at the goal I have to look at the goal, right?

139
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:56,330
It's technique, man. Here, give me the ball.

140
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:59,800
Say you're about to put the ball in the net, yeah?

141
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:04,470
Your eyes have to be on the ball and on the goal.

142
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:07,530
Before you kick, you look at the ball, then you line it up.

143
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:10,130
Look at the ball, then strike.

144
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:13,830
Beautiful.

145
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:16,800
See? / How the hell?

146
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:20,500
Not bad. You try.

147
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:24,370
Watch. Watch me. / Right.

148
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,770
Mm. / So? How was it?

149
00:16:29,770 --> 00:16:31,470
That's it? / Mm.

150
00:16:31,930 --> 00:16:32,730
Beautiful.

151
00:16:34,730 --> 00:16:39,230
So kicking a ball takes real concentration.

152
00:16:39,230 --> 00:16:41,030
Exactly, my friend.

153
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:42,900
That's how I finally understood Aof.

154
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,200
In that moment, if he'd taken the shot himself,

155
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,100
it probably would've been better than passing.

156
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:50,930
But never passing at all — can you really do that?

157
00:16:53,530 --> 00:16:56,070
Yeah, honestly you can't. / Oops.

158
00:16:56,070 --> 00:16:58,700
Look at it this way. Say you're in the middle of a match.

159
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,300
In that moment,

160
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:03,500
you have to decide for yourself what to do. / Right.

161
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:07,970
And then... / Whoa!

162
00:17:09,369 --> 00:17:11,900
Why do you want to play football anyway?

163
00:17:13,670 --> 00:17:14,970
Well, I mean...

164
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,000
You too?

165
00:17:18,069 --> 00:17:22,130
I just want to understand Aof better.

166
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,400
I have no idea what he's thinking.

167
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,970
I keep trying to understand, but...

168
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:31,530
I still don't get him.

169
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,670
Pretty sure we're not talking about football anymore.

170
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:43,900
Flirty and friendly are way too close, aren't they?

171
00:17:45,670 --> 00:17:47,270
Who could tell them apart?

172
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:52,000
He's kind to me, he gives in to me, but tells me we're only brothers.

173
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:56,200
How is my heart supposed to take that?

174
00:18:03,630 --> 00:18:05,230
This one, then.

175
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,170
Damn, that's clean.

176
00:18:27,330 --> 00:18:31,130
Fuen, that's the third card. Still haven't figured it out?

177
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:33,300
Does this have to be such a big deal?

178
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:35,830
It's a big deal to me. But I guess you wouldn't understand.

179
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:39,600
In the end you still think I'm being ridiculous.

180
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:24,070
Physics.

181
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,130
I'm sorry.

182
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:45,070
I never meant to say your feelings don't matter.

183
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:47,330
I just wasn't thinking.

184
00:19:48,630 --> 00:19:50,930
Can you forgive me?

185
00:19:54,470 --> 00:19:57,900
I'll get over it. Don't waste your time on me.

186
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:00,900
But if you want advice on winning Star over...

187
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,500
No, that's not why I came.

188
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:04,600
Since the two of you are close now,

189
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:16,070
just keep yourself in his life, quietly. That's enough.

190
00:20:42,070 --> 00:20:45,200
Hey, Physics, don't run from me.

191
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,830
Fuen.

192
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:56,770
I'm running out of patience with you.

193
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:01,270
So stay away from me for a while.

194
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:54,170
Hey, practice is this evening. Don't be late. / I'll be there.

195
00:21:54,170 --> 00:21:56,770
I'm going to rip the net open today.

196
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:03,930
Whoa, Mii. What's up?

197
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:07,700
What's wrong?

198
00:22:18,770 --> 00:22:20,770
So what are you going to do?

199
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:24,830
I know Aof wants me to break up with Rei, but I can't right now.

200
00:22:24,830 --> 00:22:26,370
Get a grip, Mii.

201
00:22:26,370 --> 00:22:28,430
Do you know who Rei's chasing these days?

202
00:22:29,030 --> 00:22:30,830
He's hitting on everyone.

203
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:36,400
You're not breaking up?

204
00:22:37,070 --> 00:22:39,300
Okay. Then wait here.

205
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:41,070
Aof, where are you going?

206
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:51,430
Right, this year's activity budget — we'll hand it over to the juniors.

207
00:22:51,430 --> 00:22:53,370
Take notes for me, please. / Okay, okay.

208
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:56,700
So there's trash-for-points, traffic duty, the mentoring program,

209
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:58,300
and the team-building activity.

210
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:00,470
And don't forget this one — the Star Contest.

211
00:23:00,470 --> 00:23:02,970
And this too, the PR page.

212
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,570
Din, tonight's event still isn't going to make it.

213
00:23:05,570 --> 00:23:07,730
You came up with another event?

214
00:23:07,730 --> 00:23:10,070
Tonight's event has nothing to do with me.

215
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,600
What are you sulking about?

216
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:14,970
He did the best he could at the time.

217
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:19,130
Yeah, I'm with Chok on this.

218
00:23:19,130 --> 00:23:21,300
Wouldn't it be easier to just ask me for help?

219
00:23:22,470 --> 00:23:25,030
You're the one who told him to handle it himself.

220
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:30,930
So this is my fault?

221
00:23:31,330 --> 00:23:32,730
No, no, no.

222
00:23:33,070 --> 00:23:34,900
It's not your fault at all.

223
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,200
But you are overdoing it, Din.

224
00:24:25,370 --> 00:24:26,930
Whatever's going on between you two

225
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:28,930
is worse than I thought.

226
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,400
I know there's nothing I can do,

227
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:37,300
but don't let it drag on.

228
00:24:39,730 --> 00:24:41,300
Yeah, I know.

229
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:43,900
Just give me some time, okay?

230
00:24:45,330 --> 00:24:47,670
Because it's not only about how I feel.

231
00:24:49,270 --> 00:24:52,330
I have to work out what I'm going to do next.

232
00:24:57,770 --> 00:25:00,170
Class.

233
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:03,330
Class, attention.

234
00:25:03,730 --> 00:25:06,200
Good morning, sir. / Good morning, sir.

235
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,170
All right, you know we've got a match today, yeah?

236
00:25:11,170 --> 00:25:13,900
No? Are you ready?

237
00:25:15,070 --> 00:25:17,930
Why so quiet? Are your heads in it?

238
00:25:18,330 --> 00:25:20,970
Are your bodies ready? / Ready, sir.

239
00:25:20,970 --> 00:25:23,430
Right, it's PE. Head ready, body ready, we've got this.

240
00:25:24,030 --> 00:25:26,030
We're playing a match today.

241
00:25:26,030 --> 00:25:27,600
I'll have you split into teams.

242
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,100
Three on three.

243
00:25:29,100 --> 00:25:31,630
Split into teams. Who doesn't have a partner yet?

244
00:25:33,830 --> 00:25:36,200
All right, we'll sort it out.

245
00:25:39,900 --> 00:25:42,400
And today we've got someone helping out.

246
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:44,600
This is Coach Nate, my teaching assistant.

247
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:46,000
Say hello to Coach Nate.

248
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,170
Hello, sir.

249
00:25:48,100 --> 00:25:50,830
Coach Nate will look after you. I've got a ministry call.

250
00:25:51,430 --> 00:25:53,100
Right, the call with the ministry.

251
00:25:53,100 --> 00:25:55,400
Of course, sir. / Go on, give it your all.

252
00:25:56,970 --> 00:25:59,930
All right, once you've got your groups, you can get up.

253
00:26:13,900 --> 00:26:15,800
Lucky Aof skipped today.

254
00:26:16,130 --> 00:26:17,600
That makes exactly three of us.

255
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,800
Here.

256
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:06,730
Pass it, I'm open.

257
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:14,670
Physics, I'm open.

258
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:33,900
Physics.

259
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:38,100
I was open. Why didn't you pass?

260
00:27:38,630 --> 00:27:40,300
You don't want me around, huh?

261
00:27:40,930 --> 00:27:42,470
Don't drag other things into this.

262
00:27:42,470 --> 00:27:44,770
You saw it. They blocked me both ways.

263
00:27:44,770 --> 00:27:47,400
Really? I ran to open up a lane for you,

264
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:50,100
and you didn't even look at me. How am I supposed to trust you?

265
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:00,730
Rei, you asshole! / What the hell is your problem?

266
00:28:00,730 --> 00:28:03,530
You again? My bad. I don't like playing off the pitch.

267
00:28:03,530 --> 00:28:06,500
Nothing against you, but what you did to my friend was fucked up.

268
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:08,330
Who? Din?

269
00:28:08,330 --> 00:28:10,830
That's hilarious. He went crying to you?

270
00:28:10,830 --> 00:28:12,130
You've got beef with Din too?

271
00:28:12,130 --> 00:28:13,700
Good, all at once, asshole!

272
00:28:14,630 --> 00:28:15,900
Fuck you, asshole!

273
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:18,000
Asshole! What are you going to do?

274
00:28:19,270 --> 00:28:20,300
Rei, you asshole!

275
00:28:22,030 --> 00:28:23,700
You son of a bitch! You son of a bitch!

276
00:28:32,870 --> 00:28:34,700
I said let's not talk right now, you and I.

277
00:28:34,700 --> 00:28:37,470
If not now, then when? Do I have to wait till we stop being friends?

278
00:28:37,470 --> 00:28:39,630
Or till we happen to run into each other again?

279
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,870
Fuen, don't put words in my mouth.

280
00:28:47,870 --> 00:28:50,730
I never said I wanted to stop being friends with you.

281
00:29:03,630 --> 00:29:05,270
Hey, what the hell is wrong with you?

282
00:29:05,630 --> 00:29:08,530
If you're angry at me, then hit me. Take it out on me.

283
00:29:08,530 --> 00:29:09,770
Hey, Fuen. / Fuen, enough.

284
00:29:09,770 --> 00:29:11,730
Hey, what the hell did I do to deserve this?

285
00:29:11,730 --> 00:29:13,130
Fuen, stop. / I'm not stopping.

286
00:29:13,130 --> 00:29:15,270
It's suffocating. He never says what's wrong.

287
00:29:15,270 --> 00:29:16,500
You're angry at me, right?

288
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:18,400
Hit me. Why take it out on him?

289
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:19,170
Hey. / Hey.

290
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:23,400
Aof, stop. Stop. Hey, stop!

291
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:26,900
Aof, stop!

292
00:29:26,900 --> 00:29:28,870
I said stop! Hey!

293
00:29:28,870 --> 00:29:30,430
If you're angry at me, then hit me.

294
00:29:30,430 --> 00:29:31,600
Hey. / Hey!

295
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:33,530
Then why take it out on the teacher?

296
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:35,330
Hey, and what about you?

297
00:29:47,930 --> 00:29:49,200
I said stop.

298
00:29:50,170 --> 00:29:51,300
Stop it, now.

299
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:53,230
He started it.

300
00:29:53,230 --> 00:29:54,530
What the hell was that?

301
00:29:54,530 --> 00:29:55,330
Hey, enough!

302
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:58,000
Leave him. You, go home. Go!

303
00:30:00,670 --> 00:30:01,670
Go home!

304
00:30:06,870 --> 00:30:08,670
Damn it, you asshole!

305
00:30:39,900 --> 00:30:41,530
Calm down.

306
00:30:53,570 --> 00:30:57,970
Rei! How are you doing?

307
00:30:58,630 --> 00:31:02,300
I don't think I can sing for you this evening, Star.

308
00:31:02,930 --> 00:31:05,170
I had a bit of an accident.

309
00:31:05,900 --> 00:31:08,000
Is it bad?

310
00:31:09,770 --> 00:31:12,070
Where are you now, Rei?

311
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:15,730
Well, I'm at the hospital.

312
00:31:16,570 --> 00:31:19,670
I'm sorry. I really didn't want it to turn out like this.

313
00:31:20,170 --> 00:31:23,100
It's all right, Rei. It was an accident either way.

314
00:31:23,970 --> 00:31:26,630
Just get better soon, Rei.

315
00:31:26,630 --> 00:31:28,130
I'm sorry.

316
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:45,600
Oww...

317
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,200
What happened?

318
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:49,430
What do we do?

319
00:31:49,430 --> 00:31:52,170
Rei's in the hospital. He had an accident.

320
00:31:53,130 --> 00:31:55,700
Who sings in Rei's place then?

321
00:31:56,030 --> 00:31:59,030
Damn, you jinxed it.

322
00:31:59,930 --> 00:32:03,100
Jinxed what? Is this the time to gloat? Help Star first.

323
00:32:03,100 --> 00:32:04,500
Or ask Din to help.

324
00:32:04,500 --> 00:32:06,430
Would he even help us?

325
00:32:28,370 --> 00:32:32,100
Damn, that's SSS tier.

326
00:32:40,870 --> 00:32:42,700
Chemi.

327
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:45,930
Stop.

328
00:32:50,770 --> 00:32:52,170
Stop right there.

329
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:16,130
Chemi, wait.

330
00:33:23,730 --> 00:33:27,400
Physics, can we talk?

331
00:33:30,870 --> 00:33:32,900
Then I'll just sit here.

332
00:33:42,070 --> 00:33:44,330
I'm sorry.

333
00:33:55,570 --> 00:33:57,770
I'm sorry too.

334
00:34:00,970 --> 00:34:02,730
For almost hitting you.

335
00:34:11,969 --> 00:34:13,600
I deserved it.

336
00:34:18,429 --> 00:34:19,929
I hurt you,

337
00:34:20,630 --> 00:34:22,130
then went looking for trouble.

338
00:34:24,199 --> 00:34:26,400
How could you deserve it?

339
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,070
Don't think like that.

340
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:39,929
Fuen.

341
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,530
Listen to me carefully.

342
00:34:56,130 --> 00:34:59,770
I like you.

343
00:35:05,730 --> 00:35:08,230
And not as a friend.

344
00:35:11,830 --> 00:35:13,900
Because I want to be more than that.

345
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:37,770
Have you ever liked me, Fuen?

346
00:35:53,500 --> 00:35:55,570
Star likes you.

347
00:35:58,530 --> 00:35:59,330
What?

348
00:36:03,070 --> 00:36:04,730
Star really likes you.

349
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:11,400
And I promised him I'd help him win you over.

350
00:36:21,470 --> 00:36:23,500
That's why I can't like you.

351
00:36:50,700 --> 00:36:53,030
Say there were no Star.

352
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:59,000
Say the two of us weren't friends.

353
00:37:01,530 --> 00:37:06,870
Say this spot right here was our whole world.

354
00:37:08,830 --> 00:37:10,770
And it was only you and me.

355
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:15,100
Would you still like me, Fuen?

356
00:37:25,830 --> 00:37:28,470
I'll give you all the time you need.

357
00:37:33,500 --> 00:37:37,300
And don't worry that I'd ever walk away from you.

358
00:37:48,070 --> 00:37:49,600
I promise.

359
00:37:50,530 --> 00:37:53,330
No matter what, I'll stay your friend.

360
00:38:12,500 --> 00:38:15,170
Physics, I...

361
00:38:27,230 --> 00:38:28,900
Stop following me.

362
00:38:28,900 --> 00:38:32,130
Come back here. / No.

363
00:38:32,130 --> 00:38:33,730
Isn't that my brother?

364
00:38:33,730 --> 00:38:34,870
I'm not singing.

365
00:38:34,870 --> 00:38:36,000
Chemi.

366
00:38:36,870 --> 00:38:38,400
Bro.

367
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:42,330
Help me out.

368
00:38:44,570 --> 00:38:46,600
What's going on?

369
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:50,870
I want to ask Chemi to sing at tonight's show.

370
00:38:51,430 --> 00:38:53,370
Doesn't Star already have a singer?

371
00:38:53,630 --> 00:38:55,800
He does, but something came up,

372
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:58,130
so we have to swap the singer last minute.

373
00:39:03,430 --> 00:39:05,100
Want to give it a shot?

374
00:39:07,430 --> 00:39:09,400
How could I?

375
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:12,330
I'd drop dead from the shock, bro.

376
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:17,570
That many people — I can't do it.

377
00:39:17,970 --> 00:39:18,770
Hey.

378
00:39:19,870 --> 00:39:23,070
And you'd let the thing you love stay just a dream?

379
00:39:42,930 --> 00:39:44,470
When you, Chemi,

380
00:39:44,900 --> 00:39:48,630
pour your heart into it and light up every time you sing.

381
00:39:50,670 --> 00:39:56,100
What happened to you was maybe just bad luck running into someone rotten.

382
00:40:08,770 --> 00:40:11,230
And people like that,

383
00:40:12,170 --> 00:40:14,800
we don't owe them anything.

384
00:40:18,830 --> 00:40:20,300
Chemi.

385
00:40:22,730 --> 00:40:25,470
Don't let one person's words

386
00:40:25,470 --> 00:40:28,130
decide your whole life.

387
00:40:32,100 --> 00:40:33,500
Want to try?

388
00:40:45,030 --> 00:40:47,430
You really think I can?

389
00:40:47,430 --> 00:40:48,400
Of course.

390
00:40:50,700 --> 00:40:52,600
And I believe

391
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:55,100
the people chasing after you believe it too.

392
00:41:09,070 --> 00:41:10,200
Well...

393
00:41:13,100 --> 00:41:14,970
I'll give it a shot.

394
00:41:15,370 --> 00:41:16,230
Yes!

395
00:41:18,330 --> 00:41:21,330
But will you sing with me?

396
00:41:21,930 --> 00:41:22,900
What?

397
00:41:25,970 --> 00:41:28,670
Sure, no problem.

398
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:46,000
Everyone, hurry up, we're running out of time.

399
00:41:48,900 --> 00:41:49,970
You all good?

400
00:42:23,030 --> 00:42:26,770
Din, are you here to lecture me again?

401
00:42:26,770 --> 00:42:29,170
We're doing our best to fix it.

402
00:42:29,170 --> 00:42:30,270
Star.

403
00:42:30,270 --> 00:42:32,300
I'm in a hurry too. / Listen to me.

404
00:42:33,870 --> 00:42:35,370
I'm not here to lecture you.

405
00:42:36,330 --> 00:42:37,800
I'm here to help.

406
00:42:42,370 --> 00:42:44,070
I called motorbike taxis for you.

407
00:42:48,370 --> 00:42:49,530
Wow.

408
00:42:52,170 --> 00:42:53,200
I get it.

409
00:42:53,200 --> 00:42:56,370
My friends and I have been through this before.

410
00:42:56,830 --> 00:42:59,600
Everyone, let's get this loaded.

411
00:42:59,600 --> 00:43:01,230
And what's left?

412
00:43:01,230 --> 00:43:04,570
Oh, the rest is up in the music room.

413
00:43:04,570 --> 00:43:07,370
We can carry it down to the bikes ourselves.

414
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:11,570
Tonnam, Chok, Tang.

415
00:43:11,570 --> 00:43:13,030
I'm counting on you.

416
00:43:14,670 --> 00:43:17,770
Ride safe, Time. The bike gets hot.

417
00:43:19,030 --> 00:43:20,600
Go on, go.

418
00:43:21,430 --> 00:43:23,370
Excuse me.

419
00:43:34,270 --> 00:43:36,470
Here, let me help.

420
00:43:36,470 --> 00:43:38,430
Thank you.

421
00:43:39,270 --> 00:43:42,200
Hey, have you got hold of FUN VIBE yet?

422
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:45,230
Oh, I'll message them right now.

423
00:43:46,030 --> 00:43:47,530
"Five more minutes. / Ours in ten."

424
00:43:47,530 --> 00:43:49,530
"Getting on now. / No ride. Taking the BTS."

425
00:43:49,530 --> 00:43:50,900
They're all on the way, Din.

426
00:43:50,900 --> 00:43:53,030
Okay, let's get going then.

427
00:44:14,430 --> 00:44:18,930
Booboo, Teu, mind how you handle it. You'll scratch it.

428
00:44:45,630 --> 00:44:48,870
How's it going? Got hold of your friends?

429
00:44:48,870 --> 00:44:52,300
Yes. They're on their way.

430
00:44:52,300 --> 00:44:56,670
They said the traffic's a bit bad. Don't worry about it, Din.

431
00:44:59,200 --> 00:45:00,730
It's fine.

432
00:45:02,270 --> 00:45:04,200
I'm sure they'll make it in time.

433
00:45:05,800 --> 00:45:07,730
Nervous, aren't you?

434
00:45:09,870 --> 00:45:11,800
Don't overthink it.

435
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:13,130
Yes, sir.

436
00:45:14,230 --> 00:45:17,170
Everything's come together nicely today.

437
00:45:18,830 --> 00:45:20,130
Just the show left now.

438
00:45:20,130 --> 00:45:22,770
Give it everything. I'll head off.

439
00:45:22,770 --> 00:45:24,930
Sure. Oh, Din?

440
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:29,800
I wanted to apologize for the other day. For the way I spoke to you.

441
00:45:30,270 --> 00:45:32,930
Forget it. I didn't take it to heart.

442
00:45:34,300 --> 00:45:38,600
But I should apologize too. For not helping from the start.

443
00:45:39,470 --> 00:45:41,000
It's really all right.

444
00:45:42,430 --> 00:45:44,970
Okay, I'll go help out backstage.

445
00:46:17,930 --> 00:46:21,100
What do we do, Star? The crowd's getting big.

446
00:46:21,500 --> 00:46:25,800
I don't know, but we've got to figure something out.

447
00:48:08,870 --> 00:48:15,000
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

448
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:18,600
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on the story of that day ♪

449
00:48:18,600 --> 00:48:26,030
♪ it warms my heart all over again ♪

450
00:48:26,030 --> 00:48:32,130
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

451
00:48:32,130 --> 00:48:36,270
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

452
00:48:36,270 --> 00:48:41,370
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

453
00:48:43,170 --> 00:48:50,630
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

454
00:48:51,970 --> 00:48:59,600
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

455
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:03,470
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

456
00:49:03,470 --> 00:49:07,730
♪ I still remember the good of us, just the same ♪

457
00:49:07,730 --> 00:49:11,870
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

458
00:49:11,870 --> 00:49:16,700
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

459
00:49:16,700 --> 00:49:20,870
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

460
00:49:20,870 --> 00:49:25,330
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

461
00:49:25,330 --> 00:49:29,470
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

462
00:49:29,470 --> 00:49:33,830
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

463
00:49:33,830 --> 00:49:39,100
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

464
00:49:39,100 --> 00:49:45,470
♪ I'm only just learning what it's like without you ♪

465
00:49:45,470 --> 00:49:49,500
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

466
00:49:49,500 --> 00:49:55,730
♪ those days make me miss you, my dear ♪

467
00:49:57,170 --> 00:50:04,900
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

468
00:50:05,630 --> 00:50:13,470
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

469
00:50:13,470 --> 00:50:17,270
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

470
00:50:17,270 --> 00:50:21,200
♪ I still remember the good of us, just the same ♪

471
00:50:21,200 --> 00:50:25,400
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

472
00:50:25,400 --> 00:50:30,030
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

473
00:50:30,030 --> 00:50:35,000
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

474
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:38,630
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

475
00:50:38,630 --> 00:50:43,000
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

476
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:48,070
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

477
00:50:48,070 --> 00:50:51,470
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

478
00:50:55,830 --> 00:51:00,100
What's wrong? Are you okay?

479
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:04,830
I'm still scared, bro. I'm nervous.

480
00:51:07,430 --> 00:51:09,700
Hey. It's all right.

481
00:51:11,070 --> 00:51:13,230
Just tell yourself you can do it.

482
00:51:13,630 --> 00:51:15,230
Trust me.

483
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:20,100
I'm nervous too, look.

484
00:51:22,600 --> 00:51:24,000
You're overdoing it.

485
00:51:24,000 --> 00:51:25,770
Come on, I really am nervous.

486
00:51:27,670 --> 00:51:28,870
Okay.

487
00:51:30,970 --> 00:51:32,530
I'll be right here.

488
00:51:35,000 --> 00:51:39,230
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

489
00:51:39,230 --> 00:51:43,430
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

490
00:51:43,430 --> 00:51:47,130
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

491
00:52:08,830 --> 00:52:12,800
Thank you all for coming out and having fun with us tonight.

492
00:52:12,800 --> 00:52:15,000
And tonight, on behalf of FUN VIBE,

493
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:18,100
I want to thank a wonderful venue like Siam Center

494
00:52:18,100 --> 00:52:21,430
for letting us put on something like this.

495
00:52:21,870 --> 00:52:25,630
Now, is everyone ready for the next song?

496
00:52:25,630 --> 00:52:26,830
Can I get a cheer?

497
00:52:35,670 --> 00:52:39,070
But tonight, FUN VIBE

498
00:52:39,070 --> 00:52:41,430
doesn't have just me on vocals.

499
00:52:46,070 --> 00:52:47,900
Because tonight,

500
00:52:48,730 --> 00:52:53,500
give it up for Physics and Chemi from Thapfah Wittayanusorn!

501
00:53:46,130 --> 00:53:48,430
Sing, kid.

502
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:53,030
I didn't memorize the words to this one.

503
00:53:53,030 --> 00:53:55,470
Can I sing the song I prepared instead?

504
00:53:55,470 --> 00:53:57,900
I did prepare one. / Hey.

505
00:53:59,070 --> 00:54:02,330
You're a singer, and you'll only sing what you like?

506
00:54:05,830 --> 00:54:09,100
I — I just... / Hey, don't argue.

507
00:54:10,370 --> 00:54:13,630
You're terrible and still hogging the spotlight.

508
00:54:47,230 --> 00:54:50,530
Nervous?

509
00:54:57,730 --> 00:54:59,870
Aof.

510
00:54:59,870 --> 00:55:01,230
And then...

511
00:55:07,370 --> 00:55:09,570
Aof, what happened to you?

512
00:55:09,570 --> 00:55:11,570
It's not that bad.

513
00:55:13,970 --> 00:55:16,970
Turns out I'm no good at comforting people.

514
00:55:17,000 --> 00:55:19,930
But you've got this tonight, Chemi.

515
00:55:25,300 --> 00:55:30,670
If you get nervous, just tell yourself you're singing this for me alone.

516
00:55:33,270 --> 00:55:38,330
I'll be waiting right over there. Look at me, and sing it for me.

517
00:55:49,170 --> 00:55:50,570
You've got this, Chemi.

518
00:56:15,630 --> 00:56:20,170
I believe you can do it, and everyone here believes it too.

519
00:56:50,970 --> 00:56:55,670
♪ There's something in my heart I can't explain ♪

520
00:56:55,670 --> 00:57:00,000
♪ Still searching for someone to tell me ♪

521
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:03,230
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

522
00:57:03,230 --> 00:57:05,670
♪ I never find what I'm looking for ♪

523
00:57:05,670 --> 00:57:09,770
♪ Why does my heart still feel so empty? ♪

524
00:57:09,770 --> 00:57:13,730
♪ I want to think it through, to find an answer ♪

